message: >-
  If you use J-Space Skills in your work, please cite this repository.
  For the underlying J-space science, please also cite Gurnee et al. (2026),
  given under preferred-citation.
title: "J-Space Skills"
abstract: >-
  Project-local Claude Code skills that add an explicit epistemic-control
  layer around Superpowers specification, planning, and implementation
  workflows: structured doubts and evidence, adversarial falsification of
  specifications and implementation plans, hash-bound skeptic reviews and
  human approvals, and deterministic promotion gates. Inspired by
  Anthropic's J-space global workspace research.
